      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\n- **I.** $y' + 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{x} \\cdot y = 3 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$\n- **II.** $y' + 3 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y = 3 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{3}$\n- **III.** $y' + x^{2} \\cdot y = \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
